Two faces of one font collection (.ttc) added to a PDF are two fonts.

pdf_find_font_resource() keyed an added font by the digest of its file, which
the faces of a collection (msgothic, simsun, cambria) share, so the second
face added got the first face's font object and drew with its glyphs and
widths. The face index is mixed into the key for faces other than the first.
(Idea from Vira Reader's mupdf-font-resource-face.patch.)

diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-resources.c b/source/pdf/pdf-resources.c
index de5d7086f..1e2fbb815 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-resources.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-resources.c
@@ -47,6 +47,20 @@ pdf_find_font_resource(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc, int type, int encodin
 
 	memset(key, 0, sizeof(*key));
 	fz_font_digest(ctx, item, key->digest);
+	/* SumatraPDF: the faces of a font collection (.ttc: msgothic, simsun,
+	 * cambria) share one file and so one digest; mix in the face index, or
+	 * the second face added gets the first one's resource (idea from Vira
+	 * Reader). */
+	if (item->subfont != 0)
+	{
+		unsigned char identity[20];
+		fz_md5 md5;
+		memcpy(identity, key->digest, 16);
+		fz_pack_uint32(identity + 16, (uint32_t)item->subfont);
+		fz_md5_init(&md5);
+		fz_md5_update(&md5, identity, sizeof(identity));
+		fz_md5_final(&md5, key->digest);
+	}
 
 	key->type = type;
 	key->encoding = encoding;
